    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4862\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Smithtown in the county\nof Suffolk, to discontinue the use of certain park land and lease such\nland for use of a wireless communications facility\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis legislation authorizes the Town of Smithtown in Suffolk County to\nlease certain parkland for the purpose of a wireless communications\nfacility.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one authorizes the Town of Smithtown to lease a portion of\nmunicipal parkland at fair-market value for a term of not more than\ntwenty-five years for the purpose of erecting, maintaining and\noperating a wireless communications facility. Proceeds realized from\nthe lease shall be used by the Town for acquisition of additional\nparklands and/or capital improvements to existing park and recreation\nfacilities.\n\nSection two provides the metes and bounds of the 3,025 square foot\nparcel (0.069 acres) which will be the subject of such lease.\n\nSection three provides for reversion of the leased parcel to the Town\nshould the lease be terminated.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Town of Smithtown has requested authorization to lease a 3,025\nsquare foot area (0.069 acres) of their municipally owned golf and\ncountry club for the erection, operation and maintenance of a wireless\ncommunication facility. The 3,025 square foot footprint is contained\nwithin the 158.50 acre golf course and is currently located behind an\nexisting maintenance building, adjacent to the municipal golf course\nat the country club. The parcel of land to be alienated is not\ncurrently utilized for any particular purpose.\n\nThe lands are to be alienated for the purpose of entering into a lease\nagreement which would authorize the construction, operation and\nmaintenance of a wireless communications facility in light of a gap in\nwireless coverage in the area. The facility will serve to enhance the\nhealth, safety and welfare of the public and visitors to the country\nclub by expanding wireless telephone service throughout the property\nand increasing the availability of emergency wireless telephone\nservice to park visitors. Additionally, the tower will be utilized for\nthe placement of public safety/emergency services antenna in order to\nimprove the reliability of radio communications in the area.\n\nAll revenue derived from the lease will be utilized by the Town to\nacquire additional parklands and/or capital improvements to existing\npark and recreation facilities.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
